 'at a finite input value' important for vertical asymptotes?","options":["Because the asymptote is a vertical line $x = x_0$ with $x_0\\in\\mathbb{R}$.","Because the divergence must happen as $x\\to\\pm\\infty$, not at a point.","Because the asymptote is a horizontal line $y = x_0$ with $x_0\\in\\mathbb{R}$.","Because $f$ must be defined and finite at the point $x_0$ itself."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"661448fa20188bf03f2c7141","time_limit":35,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_vertical_asymptote_58118087_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which condition shows that $x = 3$ is a vertical asymptote?","options":["$f(3) = 3$","$\\lim_{x\\to 3}f(x) = 0$","$f(3)$ is undefined but nearby values stay bounded.","$\\lim_{x\\to 3}f(x) = +\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6c6e4918a9e727de53ec5de3","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_vertical_asymptote_58118087_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $f(x) = \\frac{1}{x-4}$, which line is the natural candidate for a vertical asymptote based on the denominator?","options":["$x = 0$","$y = 4$","$y = 0$","$x = 4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0013d8d7242d36d455a31b84","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_vertical_asymptote_58118087_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which situation does not by itself establish a vertical asymptote at $x = x_0$?","options":["$\\lim_{x\\to x_0^+}f(x) = +\\infty$, which does establish one.","$\\lim_{x\\to x_0^-}f(x) = -\\infty$.","$f(x)$ remains bounded as $x\\t