tical asymptote?","options":["No, both sides must diverge to $+\\infty$.","No, the function must be defined at $x_0$.","Only if the function is a polynomial.","Yes, one-sided divergence is sufficient."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"13c6f699db3795ee7dd072dc","time_limit":25,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"vertical_asymptote_new_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How are vertical asymptotes detected?","options":["Using limits near the finite input.","Using only whether $f(x_0)$ is defined.","Using the zeros of the numerator of $f$.","Using limits of $f(x)$ as $x\\to\\pm\\infty$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6e0c2dc3f2a45c3765c19ad5","time_limit":25,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"vertical_asymptote_new_017","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $\\lim_{x\\to -2^-}f(x)=-\\infty$, which line is a vertical asymptote?","options":["$x=-2$","$y=-2$","$x=0$","$y=-\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"65a58fc8f1ae787f5fef3786","time_limit":20,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"vertical_asymptote_new_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $f(x)=\\dfrac{2}{x-5}$, which line is the natural vertical asymptote?","options":["$x=2$","$y=5$","$x=5$","$y=2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3ae4373a493eb6f7ee98a5b0","time_limit":20,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"}]}}